{
  "summary": "Introduces a BlockTemplateManager class to consolidate mining and block submission state and helpers, replacing free functions across the node layer. Adds a MempoolUpdated validation interface notification to asynchronously track fee-rate diagram chunk changes. Uses this tracked fee inflow in waitNext to determine whether a template has become stale without assembling full block templates on every tick.",
  "problem": "To decide whether mempool fee inflow warrants generating a new template, waitNext repeatedly locks cs_main and constructs a full block template solely to check if fee revenue increased past a threshold. Additionally, mining helper functions and template waiting utilities are scattered as free functions requiring callers to thread ChainstateManager and KernelNotifications, while SubmitBlock allocates a throwaway validation interface subscriber on each call.",
